 "notes": {
  "forAnalyst": "Order history and order detail for a signed-in shopper, plus the mutations that let them act on an order.",
  "forArchitect": "Nine schema builders over Orders. Six required dependencies and a hard line at the cart boundary: it needs XCart's chain, which is why an order Cell and a purchase Cell are usually the same host.",
  "forDeveloper": "Authorisation is the interesting part — an order query must be scoped to the caller, so extend the authorization requirements rather than the query when adding a field a customer should not see.",
  "owns": [],
  "reachForItWhen": [
   "A storefront, app or agent needs data shaped for one round trip",
   "You are extending an existing query or mutation rather than adding an endpoint",
   "The host should serve only this capability's API surface"
  ],
  "doNotReachForItWhen": [
   "Back-office CRUD — that is the module's REST controller",
   "You need a table: these modules own no schema, they compose other modules' services",
   "Bulk writes: a mutation per row is slower than the owning module's import path"
  ]
